  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(4))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(4)=-3$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(-3)=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
